# defense-messages store snapshot
# defense-type files at time of writing: 12
# defense-types: block,counter-block,counter-defy,counter-defy-wordless,counter-dodge,counter-parry,counter-quell,deflected,defy,dodge,parry,quell
# dimensions: defense-type x band(weak/normal/heavy) -- all 3 roles (actee/actor/observer)
# come from ONE coordinated RenderDefenseMessage call (same index across the triad).
# RenderDefenseMessage has no picker param (util.Rand only) -- pinned via indexOverride=0,
# the fresh-SequencePicker-first-pick equivalent for this seam.

# The melee path no longer has a banding rule of its own (M4c): internal/combat
# calls RenderDefenseMessage like every other defence. Its production-path matrix
# is frozen by internal/combat/testdata/melee_defence_bands.golden; the rows that
# used to sit here were byte-identical duplicates of the store rows above.
block|weak|actee => <ansi fg="defense-good">You barely block <ansi fg="user">Attacker</ansi>'s attack!</ansi>
block|weak|actor => <ansi fg="attack-bad"><ansi fg="mob">Defender</ansi> barely blocks your attack!</ansi>
block|weak|observer => <ansi fg="combat"><ansi fg="mob">Defender</ansi> barely blocks <ansi fg="user">Attacker</ansi>'s attack.</ansi>
